(defrule scaffolding -> scaffolding-intro scaffolding-base scaffolding-single-class scaffolding-factory scaffolding-ordering scaffolding-subagent-compile scaffolding-dependencies scaffolding-design-evolution)
(defrule scaffolding-intro -> :nucleus scaffolding-intro/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-intro/a1 :purpose scaffolding-intro/a2)
(defrule scaffolding-intro/n -> :instruction "どの時点までに何を組み上げ終えるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Before the agent can process user prompts, it must be fully assembled.")
(defrule scaffolding-intro/a1 -> :instruction "組み上げる対象を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "Every agent in OpenDev is constructed (system prompt compiled, tool schemas built, subagents registered) before the conversation lifecycle begins (Section 2.2.3).")
(defrule scaffolding-intro/a2 -> :instruction "この組み立ての道筋を知る利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "Understanding this construction pipeline clarifies why the runtime can treat all agents uniformly regardless of their role.")
(defrule scaffolding-base -> :nucleus scaffolding-base/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-base/a1 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-base/a2 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-base/a3 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-base/a4)
(defrule scaffolding-base/n -> :instruction "全エージェントの親になる型と、その引数と抽象メソッドを 1 文で書く" :sample "All agents inherit from BaseAgent, an abstract base class that accepts three constructor arguments (config, tool_registry, mode_manager) and defines four abstract methods: build_system_prompt() assembles the system prompt string, build_tool_schemas() returns OpenAI-format tool schemas, call_llm() executes a single LLM call, and run_sync() runs a full ReAct loop.")
(defrule scaffolding-base/a1 -> :instruction "設計上の肝になる決定を 1 文で書く" :sample "The critical design choice is eager construction: BaseAgent.__init__() calls both build_system_prompt() and build_tool_schemas() before the constructor returns.")
(defrule scaffolding-base/a2 -> :instruction "その結果、構築が終わった時点で何が整っているかを 1 文で書く" :sample "By the time __init__() completes, the agent is fully ready to serve requests, with no lazy prompt assembly, no first-call latency.")
(defrule scaffolding-base/a3 -> :instruction "道具が変わったときの再構築の手段を 1 文で書く" :sample "A concrete refresh_tools() method re-invokes both build methods when the tool registry changes (e.g., after MCP server discovery or dynamic skill loading).")
(defrule scaffolding-base/a4 -> :instruction "下流の部品が何に依存するかと、それで何が分かれるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Downstream code depends not on BaseAgent directly but on AgentInterface, a @runtime_checkable Protocol requiring the same surface (system_prompt, tool_schemas, refresh_tools, call_llm, run_sync), which decouples the factory from the concrete agent class.")
(defrule scaffolding-single-class -> :nucleus scaffolding-single-class/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-single-class/a1 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-single-class/a2 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-single-class/a3 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-single-class/a4 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-single-class/a5)
(defrule scaffolding-single-class/n -> :instruction "エージェントの型の階層が無いことを 1 文で書く" :sample "There is no class hierarchy of agent types.")
(defrule scaffolding-single-class/a1 -> :instruction "全てのエージェントが同じ 1 つの型の実体であることを 1 文で書く" :sample "MainAgent is the only concrete subclass of BaseAgent, and every agent in the system (the main agent, all builtin subagents, and any user-defined custom agents) is an instance of this single class.")
(defrule scaffolding-single-class/a2 -> :instruction "振る舞いの違いが何で決まるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Behavioral variation comes entirely from construction parameters: allowed_tools (a list that filters which tool schemas appear in the agent’s schema, or None for full access), _subagent_system_prompt (an override prompt set after construction), and an is_subagent flag derived from whether allowed_tools is non-null.")
(defrule scaffolding-single-class/a3 -> :instruction "構築時に準備する遅延初期化の枠を 1 文で書く" :sample "Within __init__, MainAgent sets four HTTP client slots to None for lazy initialization, one each for the normal, thinking, critique, and VLM providers, deferring API key validation until the first LLM call.")
(defrule scaffolding-single-class/a4 -> :instruction "構築時に作る部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "It creates a ToolSchemaBuilder(registry, allowed_tools) for schema generation and a bounded Queue(maxsize=10) for thread-safe message injection from the Web UI.")
(defrule scaffolding-single-class/a5 -> :instruction "遅延初期化の枠がモデルの役割とどう対応するかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The lazy client slots correspond to the model roles described in Section 2.2.5: each slot materializes a provider-specific HTTP client on first access, allowing agents to be constructed before credentials are configured.")
(defrule scaffolding-factory -> :nucleus scaffolding-factory/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-factory/a1 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-factory/a2 :elaboration-set-member scaffolding-factory/a3)
(defrule scaffolding-factory/n -> :instruction "エージェントを作る唯一の入口を 1 文で書く" :sample "AgentFactory is the single entry point for agent construction.")
(defrule scaffolding-factory/a1 -> :instruction "画面が違っても同じ手順になることを 1 文で書く" :sample "Both the TUI and Web UI invoke the same create_agents() method, ensuring identical setup regardless of frontend.")
(defrule scaffolding-factory/a2 -> :instruction "工場が踏む段階の数と順を 1 文で書く" :sample "The factory executes three phases in strict order:")
(defrule scaffolding-factory/a3 -> :instruction "段階を 1 項目ずつ、段階の名前と、その段階で何を見つけ何を登録するかで書く" :sample "Phase 1 (Skills). / Phase 2 (Subagents). / Phase 3 (Main agent)." :kind bullet)
(defrule scaffolding-ordering -> :nucleus scaffolding-ordering/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-ordering/a1)
(defrule scaffolding-ordering/n -> :instruction "段階の順序が必須である理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "The ordering constraint is essential: Phase 2 must complete before Phase 3 because the spawn_subagent tool description is dynamically built from the set of registered agents, and it must be present in the main agent’s schema.")
(defrule scaffolding-ordering/a1 -> :instruction "工場が返すものを 1 文で書く" :sample "The factory returns an AgentSuite dataclass bundling the main agent, the SubAgentManager, and the SkillLoader.")
(defrule scaffolding-subagent-compile -> :nucleus scaffolding-subagent-compile/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-subagent-compile/a1 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-subagent-compile/a2 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-subagent-compile/a3 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-subagent-compile/a4)
(defrule scaffolding-subagent-compile/n -> :instruction "部下のエージェントが最初にどんな形の仕様として書かれるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Each subagent begins as a SubAgentSpec, a TypedDict containing a name, description, system prompt, optional tool allowlist, optional model override, and optional Docker configuration.")
(defrule scaffolding-subagent-compile/a1 -> :instruction "登録するときの手順を 1 文で書く" :sample "When SubAgentManager.register_subagent(spec) is called, it executes a four-step pipeline: (1) resolve the tool list, defaulting to a hardcoded set of safe tools if none is specified; (2) create an AppConfig copy with the model override if one is provided; (3) construct a MainAgent with allowed_tools set to the resolved list, triggering the eager build of a filtered system prompt and tool schema; and (4) set agent._subagent_system_prompt to the spec’s prompt override.")
(defrule scaffolding-subagent-compile/a2 -> :instruction "その結果、何として保存されるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The result is stored as a CompiledSubAgent (name, description, agent instance, tool list).")
(defrule scaffolding-subagent-compile/a3 -> :instruction "部下の構築が安く済む理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "Construction is cheap because all subagents share the same tool registry reference, with no cloning or deep copying.")
(defrule scaffolding-subagent-compile/a4 -> :instruction "部下が分離される仕組みを 1 文で書く" :sample "Runtime isolation comes from two mechanisms: schema filtering at build time (the subagent never sees tools outside its allowlist) and message_history=None at execution time (each invocation starts with a fresh context, as detailed in Section 2.2.7).")
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies -> :nucleus scaffolding-dependencies/n :elaboration-additional scaffolding-dependencies/a1 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-dependencies/a2 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-dependencies/a3 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-dependencies/a4 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-dependencies/a5)
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies/n -> :instruction "構築の次に必要になる、実行時の部品を 1 文で書く" :sample "Agent construction produces agents; runtime execution requires services.")
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies/a1 -> :instruction "実行時の部品の入れ物が持つ項目を 1 文で書く" :sample "AgentDependencies is a Pydantic model carrying seven fields that tools need at execution time: mode_manager, approval_manager, undo_manager, session_manager, working_dir, console, and config.")
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies/a2 -> :instruction "入れ物を作って誰に渡すかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The REPL or Web UI constructs this object with all managers and passes it to agent.run_sync().")
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies/a3 -> :instruction "ループの内側でどう使うかと、その効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "Inside the ReAct loop (Section 2.2.6), individual managers are unpacked from the dependencies object and passed as keyword arguments to execute_tool(), keeping the tool registry interface flat: it does not depend on the AgentDependencies model directly.")
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies/a4 -> :instruction "部下に渡す軽い入れ物と、その項目を 1 文で書く" :sample "Subagents receive a lightweight SubAgentDeps dataclass with only three fields: mode_manager, approval_manager, and undo_manager.")
(defrule scaffolding-dependencies/a5 -> :instruction "省いた項目が作る境界を 1 文で書く" :sample "The omitted fields enforce an isolation boundary: subagents do not get session_manager (their messages are not persisted), console (output flows through ui_callback), or config (each subagent carries its own configuration from construction).")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution -> :nucleus scaffolding-design-evolution/n :elaboration-process-step scaffolding-design-evolution/a1 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-design-evolution/a2 :elaboration-process-step scaffolding-design-evolution/a3 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-design-evolution/a4 :elaboration-process-step scaffolding-design-evolution/a5 :elaboration-additional scaffolding-design-evolution/a6)
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/n -> :instruction "組み立ての設計が、どんな転換を経て今の形になったかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Three design pivots shaped the current scaffolding architecture.")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/a1 -> :instruction "1 つ目の転換で、何を何に置き換えたかを 1 文で書く" :sample "First, an early class hierarchy, with separate classes for planning agents, code-exploration agents, and web-generation agents, was replaced by the single parameterized MainAgent.")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/a2 -> :instruction "1 つ目の転換の理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "The hierarchy created a diamond problem when subagents needed mixed capabilities (e.g., a web generator that also plans), and the parameterized approach eliminated it entirely.")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/a3 -> :instruction "2 つ目の転換で、何を何に置き換えたかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Second, lazy prompt building (constructing the system prompt on the first run_sync call) was replaced by the eager-build pattern.")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/a4 -> :instruction "2 つ目の転換の理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "The lazy approach introduced first-call latency visible to the user and caused race conditions with MCP server discovery: tools registered after the first call would not appear in the prompt until a manual refresh.")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/a5 -> :instruction "3 つ目の転換で、何を何に置き換えたかを 1 文で書く" :sample "Third, inline subagent definitions, where hardcoded agent construction within the main agent’s code, were replaced by the SubAgentSpec registration system.")
(defrule scaffolding-design-evolution/a6 -> :instruction "3 つ目の転換の効果を 1 文で書く" :sample "This refactoring enabled custom agents defined in configuration files to go through the same compilation path as builtin agents, unifying the two code paths.")
